      "history_summaries": [
        "Repair round 1/3: Fixed swap_values_correct assertion by changing antecedent from `stable` to `RegNext(stable)`. Root cause: initial-state timing bug — at time 0, `stable` is true (RegNext(p)===p, RegNext(m)===m) but no swap has occurred, so prev_tmp (reset=0) doesn't equal x(m)=7. RegNext(stable) skips the first cycle, only checking after at least one cycle of stable indices has completed a swap. target_assertion_label: swap_values_correct, preserved. No homologous assertions found for this assertion_error — it's a unique timing guard issue.",
        "Repair round 2 (re-fix build): Changed `val tmp = RegInit(0.U(K.W))` to `val tmp = WireDefault(0.U(K.W))` on line 29 of swap.scala. The original Reg caused sequential semantics where `x(m) := tmp` read the stale previous-cycle tmp value instead of the newly captured x(p), corrupting the swap. A bare `Wire` failed firtool's \"sink not fully initialized\" check, so `WireDefault` provides the necessary default initialization while preserving correct combinational-forwarding semantics: within the when block, tmp gets old x(p), x(p) gets old x(m), and x(m) gets old tmp (= old x(p)) — all evaluated from pre-update values via Chisel's non-blocking assignment semantics. This fixes the causal path for both multiset_preserved (XOR no longer corrupted) and swap_values_correct (x(m) correctly receives old x(p) via tmp). Both assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
        "Repair round 3/3: Fixed swap_values_correct assertion by replacing raw `RegNext(stable)` antecedent (uninitialized, allowing formal solver to set REG=1 at time 0) with a `RegInit(false.B)` register that is explicitly assigned `REG := stable`. Root cause: the RegNext in the antecedent had no reset, so the formal solver could initialize it to 1 at time 0, making the assertion fire in the pre-swap initial state where x(p) !== prev_xm (swap hadn't happened yet). The fix initializes REG to 0 at time 0, ensuring at least one cycle of stable p,m completes a swap before checking. target_assertion_label `swap_values_correct` preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions found — this is a unique timing-guard register issue."
